# Constitution

Always-on rules for this Playwright project. Locator order, auth, cleanup, and assertion details stay in `.cursor/rules/playwright-conventions.mdc`. Routing stays in `.cursor/rules/qa-orchestration.mdc`.

## MUST

| Rule |
| --- |
| Role-based locators |
| Web-first assertions |
| storageState authentication |
| Unique, self-cleaning test data |
| Exactly one approved tag per test |

Approved tags are `@smoke`, `@sanity`, `@regression`, `@api`, `@e2e`, and `@destructive`.

## SHOULD

| Rule |
| --- |
| Faker factories |
| Enums for repeated strings |
| JSDoc on Page Object action methods |

## WON'T

| Rule |
| --- |
| XPath |
| waitForTimeout |
| Hardcoded credentials or secrets |
| TypeScript `any` |
| Weakened or removed assertions |
| Healing genuine application defects |
| Tags on `test.describe()` |

## Index

Skills: a11y-checks, api-cleanup, ci-failure-triage, explore-and-generate, exploratory-charter, jira-bug-reporter, jira-ticket-to-gherkin, network-mocking, pom-conventions, self-heal. Agents: bug-reporter, test-writer, triage.

## Agent governance

Audit the relevant rules and code before editing. Every non-trivial task produces a Proposal before the first edit: Scope, Confidence (1–10), Rationale, and Unknowns.

Confidence below 5: stop and request the missing information. Confidence 5–7: state the unknowns and wait for human approval. Confidence 8–10: proceed after the audit. Never invent a path, enum, environment variable, credential, or message. Ask or inspect the repository. This gate does not replace the human approval required before a merge or a filed Jira bug.
